# =============================================================================
# Radicale htpasswd file — EXAMPLE ONLY
# Real file: ${ROOT_DIR}/calendar/radicale/config/users
# This file MUST NOT be committed to Git. Add it to the allowlist exclusion.
#
# Format is one user per line:  username:password_hash
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW TO GENERATE THE REAL FILE — use htpasswd inside the container.
# The official image already ships apache2-utils, so this is the intended path
# and it produces a salt Radicale's autodetect recognises.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   cd /home/abed_23/apps/calendar
#   docker compose exec radicale htpasswd -B -c /etc/radicale/users abed
#   docker compose exec radicale htpasswd -B    /etc/radicale/users kamrie
#
#   -B = bcrypt. Omit -c on the second command or you will wipe the first user.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ALTERNATIVE with openssl (no container needed)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   openssl passwd -5 -salt 0123456789abcdef 'the-password'
#
#   -5 = SHA-256. THE SALT MUST BE EXACTLY 16 CHARACTERS.
#   With a shorter salt, Radicale's autodetect fails the pattern match, falls
#   back to treating the line as PLAINTEXT, and every login fails with a
#   "htpasswd/autodetect/PLAIN" warning in the log. This is silent and the
#   error message gives no hint. Verify after generating:
#
#     docker compose exec radicale cat /etc/radicale/users
#
#   Each line must look like:   abed:$5$0123456789abcdef$<43 chars>
#   If the hash after $5$ is not 16 characters long, the salt was too short.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERIFY IT WORKS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   curl -u abed:'the-password' -X PROPFIND -H 'Depth: 0' \
#        http://127.0.0.1:5232/abed/
#
#   207 = authenticated correctly.
#   401 = wrong password, or the hash fell back to plaintext.
#
# =============================================================================

# Placeholder hashes below are SHA-256 with 16-character salts, generated for
# the passwords "changeme1" and "changeme2". Do not ship these.
abed:$5$0123456789abcdef$REPLACE_ME_GENERATE_YOUR_OWN
kamrie:$5$fedcba9876543210$REPLACE_ME_GENERATE_YOUR_OWN
